      "side": 1,
      "message": "khugepaged can also remove L1 page tables (but not L2 and higher page tables). That might not be a problem here, I\u0027m not sure...\n\nAnd mremap() can move L1 and L2 page tables to a new virtual address in a new VMA, which might mean that an attacker could use mremap() to move page tables into a new VMA while they\u0027re being traversed speculatively through the old VMA, then munmap() the *new* VMA to free the page tables while they\u0027re still being traversed?\n\nAlso, what if an SPF starts on VMA 1, then VMA 1 gets concurrently merged into VMA 2 via vma_merge(), and then the entire VMA 2 is munmap\u0027ed? Or if VMA 1 gets split into VMA 1 and VMA 2, and then VMA 2 is munmap\u0027ed? I think for this to work, you might have to add something like wait_for_vma_users() to the VMA merging/splitting paths.",
